<title>USA: U.S. Cellular files $400 million debt shelf.</title>
<headline>U.S. Cellular files $400 million debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Cellular Corp filed with regulators Thursday to offer up to $400 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the company said net proceeds would go toward general corporate purposes, which may include working capital, repaying debt, future acquisitions and capital expenditures.</p>
</text>
